\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \left\{ x,y\right\} \subseteq\left[0,x^{*}\right]$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $x<y\leq x^{*}$
\end_inset

, we have 
\begin_inset Formula $y\ P\ x$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $R$
\end_inset

, then 
\begin_inset Formula $y\ P\ x\iff v(y)>v(x)$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $ $
\end_inset

 Hence, 
\begin_inset Formula $v(\cdot)$
