\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Assume 
\begin_inset Formula $R$
\end_inset

 is not continuous.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

 on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}$
\end_inset

 be represented by the utility function:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
f(x)=\left\{ \begin{array}{cc}
x & \mbox{if}\ x<1\\
x+1 & \mbox{if}\ 1\leq x\leq2\\
3-x & \mbox{if}\ 2\leq x<3\\
2-x & \mbox{if}\ 3\leq x
\end{array}\right.
\]

\end_inset

Important to note, since 
\begin_inset Formula $U(\succsim^{d},1)$
\end_inset

 is not closed, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

 is discontinuous.
 Suppose for contradiction 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

 has a utility representation 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in\left[0,x^{*}\right]:u(x)=x$
\end_inset

.
 Since 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 represents 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

, then it must be monotonically equivalent to 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

 on 
\begin_inset Formula $\left[0,x^{*}\right]$
\end_inset

.
 So, there is a monotone function 
\begin_inset Formula $\varphi:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in\left[0,x^{*}\right]:\varphi(f(x))=u(x)$
\end_inset

.
 Now, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ z\in[0,1),\ \varphi(z)=z$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ z\in[2,3],\ \varphi(z)=z-1$
\end_inset

.
 Hence, 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\leq2:u(x)=\varphi(f(x))=x$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\geq2,\ u(x)=\varphi(f(x))=4-x$
\end_inset

.
 Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $u(x)$
\end_inset

 is continuous on 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{R}_{+}$
\end_inset

.
 However, this contradicts the discontinuity of 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

.
 Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim^{d}$
\end_inset

 must not have any utility representation 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ x\in\left[0,x^{*}\right]:u(x)=x$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

