\end_inset

.
 By assumption, 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists\ \{x,y\}\subseteq\mathbb{R}_{+}^{L}:x\succ y$
\end_inset

.
 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}\equiv x$
\end_inset

.
 Now, define the function 
\begin_inset Formula $u:X\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 as follows:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
u(x)\equiv\begin{cases}
v(x) & \mbox{if}\ v(x)<v(x^{*})\\
v(x)+10 & \mbox{if}\ v(x)\geq v(x^{*})
\end{cases}
\]

\end_inset

Since 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 represents 
